.TH HIJRI 1 "September 2026" "hijri 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hijri \- convert Gregorian and tabular Hijri dates using libmuslim
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hijri
.RI [ --today " | " "--from-gregorian DATE" " | " "--to-gregorian DATE" ]
.RB [ --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert civil dates using libmuslim's arithmetic tabular Hijri calendar,
with its Friday epoch. This is not an Umm al-Qura or sighting-based calendar.
Gregorian dates are proleptic Gregorian, including before October 1582.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --today
Convert today's date in the system timezone. This is the default.
.TP
.BI "--from-gregorian " YYYY-MM-DD
Convert a Gregorian date to Hijri.
.TP
.BI "--to-gregorian " YYYY-MM-DD
Interpret the input as Hijri and convert to Gregorian.
.TP
.B --json
Print input and output objects, each with calendar and date fields.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage and examples.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version.
.SH CONVENTIONS
Exactly one conversion mode may be specified. Input must use YYYY-MM-DD,
with valid month lengths and years 0001 through 9999. Both input and output
must fit that range. Gregorian dates before 0622-07-19 produce a date before
1 AH and are rejected. Dates change at civil midnight, not sunset.
Calculated dates can differ from local religious observance.
.PP
Human output appends AH for Hijri and CE for Gregorian. JSON calendar values
are hijri and gregorian. This program does not access the network.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: success. 2: invalid usage, date or output range. 3: clock or I/O failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
hijri --from-gregorian 2024-03-11
1445-09-01 AH
hijri --to-gregorian 1445-09-01
2024-03-11 CE
hijri --today --json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prayer (1)